    {
      "url": "https://www.berwickmaine.gov/articles_T47_R953.php",
      "text": "Elections  Berwick Prepares for its November Election  Berwick voters heading to Town Hall on Tuesday, November 3rd, will find a few changes this year, including a different entrance to the polls and new ADA parking on the Sullivan Street side of the building."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.berwickmaine.gov/articles_T47_R944.php",
      "text": "Elections  Berwick Is Looking for Election Workers for November  When Berwick votes on November 3, a lot of what makes the day work will be handled by local election workers, and the Town is looking for some more people to join them."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.berwickmaine.gov/articles_T47_R875.php",
      "text": "Elections  Berwick Election Results Are In After Record June Turnout  Berwick\u2019s June election turned into a two-day count this week after more than 1,800 voters cast ballots in what town officials believe may be a record turnout for a June election in Berwick. The municipal results were signed by the Town Clerk on June 11, following a long Election Day marked by steady lines, hot weather, a nine-page ballot, and the use of an auxiliary ballot box to keep voters moving."
    },
